    "/* ---- Structs and constants: layout of the slot, slab and region tables [rt:types] ---\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Every later section reads and writes these fields. The type descriptor is the only source that knows which words are pointers at mark time (obligation 4),\n",
    " * so it is fixed before any code. */\n",
    "\n",
    "/* The reference-slot layout of a type: nptr reference fields at offsets off[k]. off points to a separate\n",
    " * uint32_t table, so the entry count has no ceiling. The allocation site hands the descriptor to the runtime with the slot, and marking walks the object's own\n",
    " * descriptor (obligation 4).\n",
    " *\n",
    " * A slot stores a **type number** (16 bits), not a descriptor pointer: a descriptor pointer is 8 bytes per slot, the largest per-slot metadata in this runtime.\n",
    " * The number-to-descriptor mapping lives in the slab's **small type table** `ttab` (deduplicated by pointer\n",
    " * equality) -- a slab is one size class, usually fed by one or two allocation sites, so a lookup is one comparison.\n",
    " * Number meaning: 0 = no descriptor (a data object, no reference fields); 1 = `EXTC_RC_CONSERVATIVE` (fallback,\n",
    " * always that one table cell); >=2 = a `ttab` index.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * EXTC_RC_CONSERVATIVE is the fallback descriptor: which words of the object are pointers is unknown, so marking scans every word of the slot\n",
    " * as a candidate pointer. It is used in one place: `alloc<T>(n)` where T has references -- the offsets of elements 1..n-1\n",
    " * change with a runtime count, which a static descriptor cannot express. Conservative marking only keeps too much, never misses. */\n",
    "typedef struct ExtcRcType {\n",
    "    uint32_t nptr;\n",
    "    const uint32_t *off;\n",
    "} ExtcRcType;\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_CONSERVATIVE ((const ExtcRcType *)-1)\n",
